MainMU [SimTalk] - AssemblyStation
Sets the number of the predecessor from which the AssemblyStation designated by <Path> pulls the main
MU.
Remarks
Specify 0 if the main part does is not delivered by any of the predecessors of the AssemblyStation, e.g. if
a Worker transports the main part to the AssemblyStation or if you use a SimTalk command to move the
main part to the AssemblyStation
As the AssemblyStation is connected to at least two stations, the order in which you connect it with the
predecessors is important. If the assembly process does not work as expected, check the numbering of the
predecessors.
Plant Simulation shows the predecessors and the successors of an object in a Tooltip when you drag the
mouse over the respective Connector.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.MainMU:integer
MainMU [SimTalk] - AssemblyStation
Plant Simulation Help 11-1815
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type integer.
Example
MyAssembly.MainMU := 1
MyAssembly.MainMU := 0 // Worker delivers main part via Workplace
See also
Main MU from Predecessor
MainMU [SimTalk] - AssemblyStation
11-1816 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

NewMU [SimTalk] - AssemblyStation
